    Bug 1933913 - Refactor TreeListbox selection to use element identity instead of index. r=darktrojan


    The `TreeListboxMixin` previously maintained selection using a `Map` keyed by
    row indices. This led to stale selection states when the DOM was mutated (e.g.,
    expanding/collapsing nodes), as indices shifted but the map keys did not.

    This patch refactors the internal selection to a `Set` of `HTMLLIElement`
    objects.

    - Selection is now anchored to the element itself, making it immune to index
      drift.
    - Added pruning logic to remove elements from selection when they are hidden or
      removed from the DOM.
    - Range selection (Shift-click) now correctly calculates against currently visible rows.
    - Escape key behavior now promotes the last interacted item.

    Test Changes:

    - Updated `subtestExpandCollapse` in `browser_treeListbox.js` to verify selection
      persistence during expansion shifts with multi-select mode enabled by
      simulating the STR of the underlying bug.

    - Fixed `doubleClick` and added `clickRow` helper functions to target the
      `firstElementChild` of row containers, ensuring mouse events hit the row
      header rather than the center of nested subtrees.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D281363

